<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Prompts used For ICL and RAG Baselines</h3>

<section id="A3.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.2.1 </span>Prompt Performance</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ C.2.1 Prompt Performance ‣ C.2 Prompts used For ICL and RAG Baselines ‣ Appendix C ‘Continual Learning of Knowledge, Styles, and Behaviors’ Experiment Details ‣ Tell Me What To Learn: Generalizing Neural Memory to be Controllable in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> we report performance across all desirata for the 5 prompts generated by GPT-5.1. We select prompt 4, as it has the highest harmonic mean. Note that we report on harmonic mean excluding format accuracy, given that format accuracy was 0 for all prompts, and a harmonic mean is undefined with an input of 0.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T7" class="ltx_table">
